# Section 3 (user interface): the start-up dialog, MRESET, OLD (prompted and stacked), SHOW and the
# defaults, the first graphics command (the device prompt kept), file output, BUILD + EXPORT.
# File output is BINARY, as in 3.2 (the RECL fix, macos e17587a1: 8 bytes x NA per record on both compilers).
# The 3.2 dialogs ran on lens_array.in and tmo.in; Dave 2026-10-19 put both in ZGD_test_files/ (tmo.in
# renamed Telescope.in, its pre-3.2 type names mapped).  OLD, the stacked OLD and SHOW run on lens_array.in
# now, INT and file output on Telescope.in (Dave re-saved it 2026-10-19, the exit pupil's zElt +91.48: the
# -91.48 of tmo.in gave a negative far-field dx the plot refused).  BUILD + EXPORT on lens_array.in as 3.2
# (`build ;`): a refused BUILD now traces, so EXPORT RAYPOS reports the chief ray (macos e17587a1).
# MODEL: 128
# TRANSCRIPT-BANNER: s03_banner
# COPY: $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/lens_array.in s03
# COPY: $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/Telescope.in s03
cd $TMP/s03
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_mreset
mreset
256
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_old
old
lens_array
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_old_stacked
old lens_array show 2
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_show_defaults
show;;
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
old Telescope
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_stretch_int +device
stretch
log10
intensity
9
/null
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_binary_int
binary
intensity
9
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
old lens_array
# TRANSCRIPT: s03_build_export
build ;
export
tex
chfr
raypos
q
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
# EXPECT: Using specified model size\s+128
# EXPECT: Enter new size \(128, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192\): \[128\]: 256[\s\S]*?Maximum pixel array size is\s+256 by\s+256
# EXPECT: Enter file name: lens_array\s+Input file lens_array\.in being loaded\.[\s\S]*?Tracing rays past\s+4 elements
# EXPECT: Elt\s+1: LensArray\s+: Conic\s+with Kc= 0\.0000D\+00, Kr=-8\.0000D-01
# EXPECT: EltName=\s+rs\s+Element=\s+Refractor[\s\S]*?KrElt=-1\.0E\+18[\s\S]*?VptElt=\s+0\.0E\+00\s+0\.0E\+00\s+2\.0000\d*E-01
# EXPECT: Enter number of element \(0=aperture\): \[0\]:\s+[\s\S]*?Wavelen=1\.0E-04[\s\S]*?Aperture=5\.0E-01[\s\S]*?nGridpts=\s+256
# EXPECT: Enter image stretch type \(LINEAR, LOG10, SQRT\): \[LINEAR\]: log10
# EXPECT: Graphics device/type \(\? to see list, default /xw\):/null
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 2\.8304\d*D\+02; Peak occurs at i=\s+129, j=\s+129\s+Sum of intensity= 1\.9163\d*D\+03
# EXPECT: Plot type set to BINARY[\s\S]*?DIRECT ACCESS File=Telescope\.int9\s[\s\S]*?Binary array is of dimension\s+256 by\s+256
# EXPECT-NOT: plot bounds are degenerate
# EXPECT: Exporting data to lens_array\.txt[\s\S]*?% RayPos 3-vectors for\s+1 rays at Element\s+1
# EXPECT-NOT: Write exceeds length
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
